  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the accusation scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the accusation scene, where the meme presents a false narrative that the woman married her brother to commit immigration fraud, making her an illegal alien and calling for her deportation. The user is implicitly positioned as someone who should take action (e.g., call ICE) or who is being urged to believe the false accusation. The text 'ice, where are you?' directly addresses the user, inviting them to act or to be part of the call for deportation, thus projecting the user onto the scene as an active participant in the hostile narrative.",
